#: includes/class-privacy.php:27
msgid "Suggested text. Review it and adapt it to how you use the plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:28
msgid "Only users with the Board editor role, editors and administrators can pin notes and photos to a pinboard on this site. For every note we store the user ID of the author, the note text, its position and tilt on the board, the sticky flag and its creation date. Uploaded images are stored in the media library as attachments with the uploader as author; before storage they are re-encoded to remove EXIF and GPS metadata, and they are given random file names."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:29
msgid "Visitors see the notes but the names of their authors are never shown to guests. The plugin does not store IP addresses, does not set its own cookies and does not use external services. The limit on new notes per hour is based on the user ID only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-privacy.php:30
msgid "Notes expire after the lifetime configured for the board unless they are marked sticky. Expired notes are hidden immediately, moved to the trash by a daily job and permanently deleted together with their images when WordPress empties the trash (after 30 days by default). On request, notes and images of a user are included in the personal data export and are deleted by the personal data erasure of WordPress. If the email notification of a board is enabled, an email with the note title and the display name of the author is sent to the site administrator."
msgstr ""

